acts/preflight/001-preflight.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-05T01:50:55.889Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-05T01:50:56.997Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:53:2. **Treated self-review's `specDeviations` as disclosure rather than a routing signal.** When a self-review pass declares a spec deviation, that is the implementor admitting it did not finish the integration. The correct response is `story-continue` with a bounded follow-up, not \"noted.\" The skill's fix-routing doc is explicit: declared deviations and blocking verifier findings route to same-session follow-up.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:54:3. **Treated convergent verifier findings as debatable opinions.** Two fresh verifiers independently flagging the same integration gap with `blocking: true` is the strongest signal the CLI produces. Overriding it requires tech-design evidence against the verifiers' interpretation, not scope-argument rationalization.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:158:- 06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:172:### 06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states (accepted 2026-04-24 ~02:55Z)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:198:- Acceptance Rationale: All real findings from rounds 1-2 fixed. Round 3 findings are environment false positives — convergent format-drift from verifier codex sessions (not present in actual working tree), V1-only client test failures not reproduced by V2 or orchestrator. Orchestrator independent gate runs pass clean on all lanes. Baseline +52 with no regressions. Durable reopen, unavailable states, bounded degraded rendering, stale-selection guards, and explicit-member unavailability all integrated per tech design.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:202:### 06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states (accepted 2026-04-24 ~09:00Z)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:234:- Story Title: Story 5: Package Export (two-phase)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:269:  - (rd 6) V2 minor bootstrap error taxonomy (review-workspace GET fallback misclassifies as export failure) → **defer to cleanup batch** (Epic 4 cleanup — trivial one-liner; not Story 5 scope despite being in touched files)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:276:- Acceptance Rationale: Story 5 has the widest surface in Epic 4 — every round surfaced adjacent concerns that narrow prompts didn't preempt (documented self-critique above). After 5 follow-ups all dispatched via `story-continue` (no wrong-channel quick-fix routing this time), round 6 produced zero blocking findings and V2 clean. Real `.mpkz` streaming + signed URL + client UX + aria-live + per-package state isolation all integrated per tech design. Deferred items are Story 6 / cleanup scope.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:416:- Acceptance Rationale: 3 verifier rounds, real Convex package read path now integrated end-to-end with seeded-snapshot integration test, unsupported-kind fallback integrated, cross-kind target ordering integrated, 0 real Story 1 blocking findings remain. The only remaining `blocking` verifier finding is a flaky pre-existing integration test that passes on re-run and that V1 saw as pass. Baseline up +28 with no regressions. Original \"shim\" acceptance corrected.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/team-impl-log.md:496:| 06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states | 488 | 541 | +53 | +4 new test files (nfr, observability, a11y, bundle-budget), +production a11y/observability wiring, +selectio