8.237Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:11:| `tech-design-client.md` | Review route, workspace page composition, markdown render container, client-side Mermaid with placeholder hydration, version switching, degraded-state rendering |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:24:Epic 4 is designable, with one correction already applied and two clarifications captured below. The spec now anchors the export format to the Liminal Build markdown package (`.mpkz`) primitive, keeps review entry tied to the existing process-surface `review` action, and separates bounded degraded-target failures from request-level errors.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:218:The unsupported path is a bounded degraded state, not a hard error. The review target still loads (`status: unsupported`), the review workspace stays open, navigation continues to work, and the user sees enough to tell that a reviewable version exists but isn't renderable in this release. `REVIEW_TARGET_UNSUPPORTED` is the error-code label inside the bounded failure envelope.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:222:The failure boundary sits one level below the review workspace envelope. Request-level errors (401, 403, 404, 503) apply only to resolution and authorization — the response cannot be produced at all. Once project identity, process identity, and target identity resolve, the response always returns 200 with the review workspace envelope populated. Problems *inside* that envelope surface as bounded degraded states on specific fields:\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:224:- `target.status = error | unsupported | unavailable` with a populated `target.error` record when the whole target is degraded (unsupported format, render failure, artifact unavailable)\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:436:        ├── degraded-state.ts\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:529:| Chunk 6 | Reopen and degraded review states: durable reopen across all target kinds, unavailable/forbidden handling on direct review URLs, bounded render failure envelope on reload, accessibility verification | AC-6.1 through AC-6.3 | review workspace service, client router + bootstrap, degraded-state rendering, A11y manual verification |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:543:- no reopen/degraded guarantees before the durable shapes are complete\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:23:| AC-3.4 | TC-3.4a | Story 3 | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | One degraded archive entry does not hide healthy entries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:28:| AC-5.1 | TC-5.1a | Story 5 | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | Structural derived view returned without generated summary text |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:29:| AC-5.2 | TC-5.2a | Story 5 | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | View metadata identifies turn range and archive-entry references |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:30:| AC-5.3 | TC-5.3a, TC-5.3b | Story 5 | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` | Views preserve provenance back to turns and archive entries |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:31:| AC-5.4 | TC-5.4a | Story 5 | `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` | Derived-view creation does not replace archive rows |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:32:| AC-5.5 | TC-5.5a, TC-5.5b | Story 5 | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | Derived-view failure leaves archive readable and reports degraded state |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:52:| Path 4.1 | User requests structural derived views over turns | Story 5 | TC-5.1a, TC-5.2a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:53:| Path 4.2 | Derived views trace to source turns and source archive entries without replacing archive truth | Story 5 | TC-5.3a, TC-5.3b, TC-5.4a | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`; `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:54:| Path 4.3 | Derived-view failure returns degraded state while archive remains readable | Story 5 | TC-5.5a, TC-5.5b | `tests/service/server/derived-archive-view.test.ts`; `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/coverage.md:65:- Integration path trace covers capture, finalization/live separation, archive read/reopen, turn derivation, structural derived views, provenance enrichment, degraded-state isolation, and bounded long-process reads.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/00-foundation/007-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"0b8e2adf-819c-4b34-8a0f-ef03f7bce188\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df5ec-e2d5-7f43-89e4-9f925457a84f\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df5ec-e2d5-7f43-89e4-9f925457a84f\",\"storyId\":\"00-foundation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"00-foundation\",\"title\":\"Story 0: Foundation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/00-foundation.md\",\"docs/spe