ier findings.\\\",\\\"acceptanceCheckRefs\\\":[\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/00-foundation/003-implementor.json\\\",\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/00-foundation/005-verify.json\\\"],\\\"acceptanceChecks\\\":[{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Definition of Done coverage\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier confirmed shared contracts define repository identity, source attachment summaries, provenance entries, refresh/detach responses, route params/path constants, and source-management error codes.\\\",\\\"Verifier confirmed Convex schema/index seams cover repositoryFullName duplicate keys, four-state hydration, refresh metadata, and soft-detach durability.\\\",\\\"Verifier confirmed provenance durability copies immutable repository identity separately from current attachment enrichment state.\\\",\\\"Verifier confirmed reusable fixtures cover four-state freshness, pending refresh, soft detach, process shadowing, missing-target-ref duplicate handling, unavailable sources, and degraded provenance.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The verifier mapped the implemented files and tests directly to the Story 0 Definition of Done and found no gaps.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Non-TC decided test coverage\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier confirmed automated contract tests verify expanded source schemas and reject missing Epic 6 identity/freshness fields.\\\",\\\"Implementor added tests/service/server/source-management-contracts.test.ts and updated tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts plus Convex/source fixture coverage.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"Story 0 owns shared contract/schema/fixture coverage rather than end-user TC behavior, and the durable record contains the required non-TC proof.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Verification gates\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier ran corepack pnpm run green-verify with result pass.\\\",\\\"Verifier ran corepack pnpm run verify-all with result pass.\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"The configured story gate and epic gate both passed in the independent verifier result.\\\"},{\\\"name\\\":\\\"Open findings\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Verifier reported newFindings: [], openFindings: [], and unverified requirement coverage: [].\\\"],\\\"reasoning\\\":\\\"There are no unresolved verification findings requiring quick-fix, ruling, block, or another verification pass.\\\"}],\\\"recommendedImplLeadAction\\\":\\\"accept\\\"},\\\"verification\\\":{\\\"finalVerifierOutcome\\\":\\\"pass\\\",\\\"findings\\\":[]}}\"}}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/002-story-orchestrate-run.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate run\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"completed\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"storyRunId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHistoryPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\",\"finalPackagePath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-final-package.json\",\"finalPackage\":{\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyRunId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"attempt\":1,\"summary\":{\"storyTitle\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\",\"implementedScope\":\"Replaced the fake immediate-refresh success path with a runtime-backed hydration executor that resolves a real process working-copy target, uses the provider adapter hydration/rehydration seam, returns pending/failed/not-available truthfully, and only marks a source hydrated after actual runtime refresh completion.\",\"acceptanceRationale\":\"Story-lead is pausing for caller ruling 03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001-ruling-018 before impl-lead can accept the story.\"},\"evidence\":{\"implementorArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/003-implementor.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"implementor-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/005-continue.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"selfReviewArtifacts\":[],\"verifierArtifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"},{\"kind\":\"verifier-result\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"provenance\":\"current-run\"}],\"quickFixArtifacts\":[],\"callerInputArtifacts\":[],\"gateRuns\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}]},\"verification\":{\"finalVerifierOutcome\":\"block\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"]}]},\"riskAndDeviationReview\":{\"specDeviations\":[{\"description\":\"Project-scoped sources without a single unambiguous current process working-copy target no longer get a fabricated settled refresh; they now return request-level refresh-not-available until a real runtime target exists.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story implementor surfaced this spec deviation during bounded child execution.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/003-implementor.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/005-continue.json\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"needs-ruling\",\"approvalSource\":null}],\"assumedRisks\":[],\"scopeChanges\":[],\"productionPathDecisionItems\":[{\"description\":\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null}]},\"diffReview\":{\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts\",\"reason\":\"Replaced the immediate-success stub with a runtime hydration executor, real process target resolution, provider-adapter refresh execution, and truthful settled/pending/failed/not-available handling.\"},{\"path\":\"apps/platform/server/app.ts\",\"reason\":\"Wired production source refresh to the real provider-adapter registry via RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.\"},{\"path\":\"tests/service/server/source-management-api.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Added production-path refresh tests proving the route uses the runtime provider seam and does not mark sources hydrated when refresh fails.\"},{\"path\":\"tests/service/server/source-management-service.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"Updated refresh-service test construction for the new non-default executor requirement.\"}],\"storyScopedAssessment\":\"Latest bounded child-operation changes remain scoped to the active story.\"},\"acceptanceChecks\":[{\"name\":\"story-gate-result\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\"],\"reasoning\":\"Story gate corepack pnpm run verify-all reported pass.\"},{\"name\":\"final-verifier-result\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\"],\"reasoning\":\"Final verifier outcome is block.\"},{\"name\":\"unresolved-findings-status\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"The story/design says project-scoped actions appear in the project source section and Story 3 includes refresh/rehydration for `stale` and `not_hydrated` attachments. In the client, `renderSourceAttachmentSection()` renders refresh controls for any source whose hydration state is `stale` or `not_hydrated` regardless of scope (`apps/platform/client/features/projects/source-attachment-section.ts`). In the new runtime path, `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor.resolveTargetProcessId()` returns `null` for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source, and `refreshRecoverableSource()` then returns `kind: 'not_available'` with message `no single current process working copy owns this source attachment` (`apps/platform/server/services/sources/source-refresh.service.ts`). The modified API tests only verify successful refresh for process-scoped attachments; no server or client test proves the project-scoped case or suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"],\"reasoning\":\"1 verifier finding(s) remain unresolved.\"},{\"name\":\"scope-change-status\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[],\"reasoning\":\"No scope changes require further ruling.\"},{\"name\":\"production-path-status\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"reasoning\":\"No production-path