r suppresses the project-shell control when the backend will 409. This leaves project-scoped recoverability behavior unresolved and can present a false recovery path on the project shell.\"]}],\"baselineBeforeStory\":611,\"baselineAfterStory\":613,\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cumulativeBaseline\":{\"baselineBeforeCurrentStory\":611,\"expectedAfterCurrentStory\":613,\"latestActualTotal\":613},\"commitReadiness\":{\"state\":\"not-ready\",\"reason\":\"Caller ruling is still required before impl-lead commit.\"},\"openRisks\":[\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\",\"Verification finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity remains unresolved.\"]},\"cleanupHandoff\":{\"acceptedRiskItems\":[],\"deferredItems\":[{\"description\":\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production no longer uses the prior fake immediate-success executor: `createApp` now injects `RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor`, and the focused API tests show refresh invoking real provider-adapter hydration methods and preserving non-hydrated state on runtime failure.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null},{\"description\":\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\",\"reasoning\":\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\",\"evidence\":[\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/004-verify.json\",\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/006-verify.json\",\"Production refresh now has a new scope ambiguity for project-scoped attachments: the backend requires exactly one current owning process, while the project-shell UI still offers refresh purely from `stale`/`not_hydrated` state, so some project-scoped rows can advertise a recovery path that immediately returns `SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE`.\"],\"approvalStatus\":\"not-required\",\"approvalSource\":null}],\"cleanupRequired\":true},\"rulingRequest\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management-story-run-001-ruling-018\",\"decisionType\":\"project-scoped-refresh-semantics\",\"question\":\"For project-scoped source attachments shown in the project shell, what should refresh do when the attachment is stale or not_hydrated but there is no single unambiguous current process working-copy target?\",\"defaultRecommendation\":\"Hide or disable the project-shell refresh control unless the backend can identify exactly one current process working-copy target; keep refresh enabled for process-scoped rows and for project-scoped rows with one unambiguous owning process. This avoids falsely promising recovery and aligns with AC-3.2 until a later story defines cross-process/project-level hydration semantics.\",\"evidence\":[\"Verifier finding story-3-project-scope-refresh-target-ambiguity is blocking and affects AC-3.2, AC-3.3, TC-3.2a, TC-3.2c, and TC-3.3a.\",\"Client project source section renders refresh controls for any stale or not_hydrated source regardless of scope.\",\"RuntimeSourceHydrationExecutor returns SOURCE_ATTACHMENT_REFRESH_NOT_AVAILABLE for project-scoped attachments unless exactly one current process references the source.\",\"All gates passed, but verifier outcome is needs-human-ruling because story-local requirements do not define project-scoped refresh target selection.\"],\"allowedResponses\":[\"Disable/hide project-shell refresh unless a single current process target exists; continue implementation to make UI truthful.\",\"Define project-scoped refresh to automatically select or create a runtime target; continue implementation with that behavior.\",\"Treat project-scoped refresh ambiguity as out of scope for Story 3 and allow current backend rejection despite the visible UI control.\",\"Block Story 3 until a separate design update defines project-scoped refresh semantics.\"]},\"recommendedImplLeadAction\":\"ask-ruling\"}},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"story-run-current\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-current.json\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-events\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-status\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/progress/001-story-lead.status.json\"},{\"kind\":\"story-run-final-package\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/story-lead/001-final-package.json\"},{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/007-story-orchestrate-status.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:16:42.922Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-05-04T20:16:42.934Z\"}\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/artifacts/03-hydration-and-freshness-management/010-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"fcb5202c-4d3c-4874-baa5-c7b50776685e\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.4\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019df48d-74e0-7b10-8cd1-5c81de53be12\",\"storyId\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\"},\"mode\":\"followup\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-hydration-and-freshness-management\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Hydration and Freshness Management\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/stories/03-hydration-and-freshness-management.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/test-plan.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/a