pec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-158-| Process-scoped attach updates current process source refs immediately | The epic says a process-scoped attachment belongs to one process as current source state and becomes visible immediately | `attachProcessSource` persists the source row and adds its id to that process's current source refs in the same orchestration path |\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:159:| Process scope shadows project scope only in current-source reads | Same repo can be useful both project-wide and process-specific | Durable rows can coexist; resolver picks process-scoped row for that process when identity/ref collide |\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-160-| Read-write attachments require branch-like target refs | Durable code updates need a writable moving ref rather than an immutable commit/tag | `read_write` attachments reject tag/commit target refs; `read_only` attachments may use branch/tag/commit |\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-161-| Provenance records copy immutable identity | Detach or access loss must not erase process history | Provenance stores `repositoryFullName`, `repositoryUrl`, `targetRef`, relationship kind, and optional attachment id |\\\\n--\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-185-├── source-management.service.ts                 # NEW: orchestration, validation, conflict/shadowing policy\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md-186-├── source-identity.service.ts                   # NEW: URL parsing, canonical full-name derivation, target-ref normalization\\\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/06--source-attachments-and-canonical-source-management/tech-design.md:187:├── g