\\\n| Shared live update contract | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Fixtures: ready/empty/error for all sections | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Fixtures: live-update messages across all entity types | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: bootstrap rendering | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: live-update application | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: reconnect reconciliation | PARTIALLY SATISFIED — state fixture + dedup logic exist; no exported reconciliation helper function |\\\\n| No user-visible Story 1+ behavior | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared vocabulary single-sourced | SATISFIED |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST DIFF AUDIT\\\\n\\\\nThe git diff glob returned empty (likely path expansion mismatch); the file was verified directly. `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` contains exactly two tests:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Rejects mismatched processId vs payload.processId** — schema-level `superRefine` throws with `/payload\\\\\\\\.processId/i`\\\\n2. **Ignores cross-process message in apply helper** — `applyLiveProcessMessage` returns the state reference unchanged\\\\n\\\\nBoth match bundle claims. Base commit did not contain this test file.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX GUIDELINE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #1 — normalization: CONFIRMED CLOSED.**\\\\n`git show c9a63ef:convex/processes.ts` line 1 reads `mutationGeneric as mutation, queryGeneric as query`. Current code imports from `./_generated/server.js`. All handlers use typed `ctx.db` with bounded `.take(200)`.\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #2 — \\\\\\\"duplicate index removed\\\\\\\": CLAIM INACCURATE.** **(MAJOR)**\\\\n\\\\nThe base commit had:\\\\n```\\\\n.index('by_projectId', ['projectId'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe current code has:\\\\n```\\\\n.index('by_projectId', ['projectId'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWhat happened: the compound index was **renamed** (`by_projectId_updatedAt` → `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`). No index was removed. Both non-duplicate indexes remain. The bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is a documentation inaccuracy — not a correctness defect.\\\\n\\\\nThe `by_projectId` simple index appears unreferenced within `processes.ts` (the query uses the compound index). Worth grepping across all convex files before Story 1.\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #3 — cross-process live upsert hole: CONFIRMED CLOSED.**\\\\n`processLiveDataMessageSchema` has a `superRefine` checking `value.payload.processId !== value.processId`. `applyLiveProcessMessage` guards `args.state.processId !== args.message.processId`. Both layers present. Test 1 exercises the schema guard; Test 2 exercises the reducer guard.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT AND FIXTURE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `z.union` used instead of `z.discriminatedUnion` for `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema` — functionally correct, but produces less targeted parse errors.\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `completedAt` is nullable at schema level for all message types including `complete` — no enforcement that complete messages carry a timestamp.\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` intentionally excludes `'open'` and `'rehydrate'` that exist in the shell enum. Valid design, but later story authors need to know which enum applies.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nNone.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is inaccurate.** Rename happened; nothing removed.\\\\n2. **`by_projectId` index may be dead.** Grep before Story 1; remove if unreferenced.\\\\n3. **`websocketPlugin` does not register `@fastify/websocket`** — intentional Story 0 scaffolding, but Story 2/3 implementers must add the actual registration.\\\\n4. **`bootstrap.ts` still calls `getProjectShell` for `process-work-surface` routes** — Story 1 must address or tolerate this.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE RESULT\\\\n\\\\nApproval required to run shell commands. Bundle claims both typecheck and build passed. Schema coherence is confirmed structurally by file reads (all types align, all schemas parse in fixture constructors). No typecheck errors visible in code.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Noticed but not reported\\\\n\\\\n- `isStaleMessage` treats messages from a different `subscriptionId` as **not stale** (returns `false` when IDs differ). Semantically this means old-subscription messages pass through — a potential reconnect-coherence gap in Story 2+.\\\\n- `processUpsertLiveFixture` uses a different process ID than `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` without the naming making this obvious. Later test authors could be confused.\\\\n- Health endpoint label `'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'` is stale — not Story 0's code to change, but misleading.\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3b64d224-e648-4c11-9534-cfdf540431d0\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.0675963499999999,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":210,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":83943,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":1422967,\\\"output_tokens\\\":21686,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":83943,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":8,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1367,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":90851,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":5501,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":5501},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":210,\\\"outputTokens\\\":21686,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":1422967,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":83943,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.0675963499999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01Hombj7z7xmf1CWdgP3u5za\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck 2>&1 | tail -20\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":120000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01DQ5a8Mi6d5kWE8f74j7TzB\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":120000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck acceptance gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_017ujYpSg7T9fbPMgb6NyBbC\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review-round-2.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Sonnet Review: Story 0 Foundation Round 2\\\\n\\\\n- **Reviewer model:** claude-sonnet-4-6\\\\n- **Review date:** 2026-04-14\\\\n- **Story base commit:** `c9a63ef2b71e7bdfa380a6c7313f3a2b38e7c9ac`\\\\n- **Bundle reviewed:** `story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle-round-2.md`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: PASS\\\\n\\\\nOne bundle claim is materially inaccurate (documented below as MAJOR). No claim misrepresents the correctness of the code itself — the inaccuracy is in the description of what changed, not in whether the round-1 hole is closed. The implementation is functionally sound, within Story 0 boundaries, and ready for Story 1 build.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY 0 REQUIREMENTS MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route and endpoint naming for the process work surface | SATISFIED | `process-work-surface.ts` exports all six URL patterns and four path builders; `router.ts` correctly orders process-route match before project-shell match |\\\\n| Shared process status, action, history-item, and live-update vocabulary | SATISFIED | `processStatusSchema`, `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`, `processHistoryItemKindSchema`, `processHistoryItemLifecycleSchema`, `liveProcessMessageTypeSchema`, `liveProcessEntityTypeSchema` all defined in shared contracts; vocabulary matches Story 0 spec table exactly |\\\\n| Shared section error contract | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceSectionErrorSchema` with typed `code` enum (`PROCESS_SURFACE_HISTORY_LOAD_FAILED`, etc.) and non-empty `message` |\\\\n| Shared live update contract | SATISFIED | `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` covers all nine required fields; entity-specific discriminated schemas enforce payload typing per entity type |\\\\n| Reusable fixtures covering ready, empty, and error section envelopes | SATISFIED | `process-history.ts`, `materials.ts`, `side-work.ts` each export all three section states; confirmed via schema parse validation in fixture file |\\\\n| Reusable fixtures for live-update messages | SATISFIED | `live-process.ts` exports fixtures for all five entity types (`process`, `history`, `current_request`, `materials`, `side_work`) across all message types; state fixtures for connected and reconnecting states |\\\\n| Test helpers: bootstrap rendering | SATISFIED | `render-shell.ts` supports arbitrary pathname overrides including process-surface routes; `bootstrap.ts` seeds `processSurface.projectId` and `processSurface.processId` from route parse |\\\\n| Test helpers: live-update application | SATISFIED | `process-live.ts` exports `applyLiveProcessMessage` covering all entity branches and stale-message guard |\\\\n| Test helpers: reconnect reconciliation scenarios | PARTIALLY SATISFIED | `reconnectingProcessSurfaceStateFixture` in `live-process.ts` and `mergeHistoryItems` deduplication in the apply helper exist; no explicit reconciliation helper function exported for later stories to call directly |\\\\n| Story 0 introduces no user-visible behavior conflicting with Stories 1–6 | SATISFIED | `registerProcessRoutes` is a no-op; `NotImplementedProcessWorkSurfaceService` throws 501; `NoopProcessLiveHub` does nothing; `ProcessModuleRegistry` initialises empty |\\\\n| Story files and coverage artifacts can reference foundation without redefining shared vocabulary | SATISFIED | `index.ts` re-exports all four contract modules; vocabulary is single-sourced |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST DIFF AUDIT\\\\n\\\\n**Confirmed by direct file read.** `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` contains exactly two tests:\\\\n\\\\n1. `rejects process messages whose top-level process id differs from the payload process id` — calls `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema.parse()` with mismatched `processId`/`payload.processId`; expects throw matching `/payload\\\\\\\\.processId/i`. Matches bundle claim #1.\\\\n\\\\n2. `ignores process messages for another process surface` — constructs a valid cross-process message, applies it via `applyLiveProcessMessage` to `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` (different `processId`), asserts referential identity (`toBe`). Matches bundle claim #2.\\\\n\\\\n**Git diff note:** The shell command `git diff c9a63ef -- \\\\\\\"*.test.*\\\\\\\"` returned empty. Most likely cause: the glob did not expand to include the test file path (globbing semantics in git differ from shell). The test file was verified directly via file read; its content is consistent with the bundle's \\\\\\\"Changed Test Files\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Tests Added Or Updated\\\\\\\" sections.\\\\n\\\\n**Test count from base commit:** The base commit did not contain `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` (confirmed: it appears in `git status` as untracked relative to the working tree starting from `c9a63ef`). Round 2 added two new tests. No existing tests were deleted or modified.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT AND FIXTURE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F1 — `processSurfaceSummarySchema` uses a narrower action enum than `processSummarySchema`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` = `['start', 'respond', 'resume', 'review', 'restart']`. The Epic 1 shell uses `processAvailableActionSchema` = `['open', 'respond', 'resume', 'review', 'rehydrate', 'restart']`. The two schemas are intentionally separate — the shell uses `open` and `rehydrate`; the surface does not. Story 0 spec table lists exactly `start, respond, resume, review, restart`.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `schemas.ts:23–31` and `process-work-surface.ts:55–62`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** Maybe the two enums should merge. They don't — `open` is a shell-level navigation action, not a surface-level action. The design distinction is valid.\\\\n- **Impact:** None now; later stories must be aware they draw from `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`, not from the shell enum.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Confirm Story 1+ fixtures use `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` actions only.\\\\n\\\\n### F2 — `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema` uses `z.union` rather than `z.discriminatedUnion`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** The six branches are combined via `z.union(...)`. Because `entityType` + `messageType` together fully discriminate every branch, a `z.discriminatedUnion` on `entityType` (with a nested union for the error case) would be marginally more efficient and produce clearer parse errors.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `live-process-updates.ts:89–97`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** `z.union` is functionally correct and all union members are properly ordered (error message last). Parse errors may be less targeted, but Story 0 tests confirm correct acceptance/rejection behavior.\\\\n- **Impact:** Slightly noisier parse errors in future debugging. No correctness impact.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Future story review may want to migrate to discriminated union for parse-error quality, but not a Story 0 blocker.\\\\n\\\\n### F3 — `completedAt` nullable for all message types including `complete`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` defines `completedAt: z.string().min(1).nullable()`. A `complete` message can therefore parse successfully with `completedAt: null`. The Story 0 spec says `completedAt` should be \\\\\\\"ISO 8601 UTC when present\\\\\\\". There is no schema-level enforcement that `complete` messages must carry a non-null `completedAt`.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `live-process-updates.ts:32`, `live-process.ts:67–77` (fixture sets `completedAt` in `historyCompleteLiveFixture` and `currentRequestClearedLiveFixture`, so the pattern is demonstrated but not enforced)\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** The tech design describes `completedAt` as \\\\\\\"when present\\\\\\\" — an optional field that signals completion timing but is not required. Story 0 fixtures correctly set it on complete messages. Schema enforcement is Story 1+ territory.\\\\n- **Impact:** Consumers of `complete` messages must null-check `completedAt` themselves.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Acceptable at Story 0 level.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX GUIDELINE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F4 — `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric` imports removed; typed imports confirmed\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Base commit `convex/processes.ts` imported `mutationGeneric as mutation` and `queryGeneric as query` from `'convex/server'`. Current code imports `mutation` and `query` from `'./_generated/server.js'`. All handlers now use typed `ctx.db` with proper Convex return types.\\\\n- **Severity:** N/A (fix confirmed)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `git show c9a63ef:convex/processes.ts` (line 1 shows `mutationGeneric`); current `processes.ts:4` shows `from './_generated/server.js'`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** None — the before/after is deterministically visible in git.\\\\n- **Impact:** Round-1 finding confirmed closed.\\\\n\\\\n### F5 — `currentRequestHistoryItemId` field added to `processesTableFields`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Base commit `processesTableFields` did not include `currentRequestHistoryItemId`. Current code adds `currentRequestHistoryItemId: v.union(v.id('processHistoryItems'), v.null())`. This is correctly typed as a Convex ID reference, not a raw string. The `createProcess` mutation initialises it to `null`.\\\\n- **Severity:** N/A (correct addition)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `processes.ts:29`, `processes.ts:65`\\\\n- **Impact:** Story 2 (current request projection) can locate the pinned request via this pointer.\\\\n\\\\n### F6 — `processes` table retains `by_projectId` index alongside `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Current schema has two indexes on `processes`: `by_projectId` (`['projectId']`) and `by_projectId_and_updatedAt` (`['projectId', 'updatedAt']`). The base commit also had two indexes, with the compound one named `by_projectId_updatedAt`. The only change was a **rename** of the compound index (`by_projectId_updatedAt` → `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`). **No index was removed.** The bundle claims \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" — this is inaccurate.\\\\n- **Severity:** MAJOR (bundle claim inaccuracy, not a code defect)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `git show c9a63ef:convex/schema.ts` shows both `by_projectId` and `by_projectId_updatedAt` indexes; current `schema.ts:23–25` shows `by_projectId` and `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** Maybe the rename was an intentional partial fix and the full \\\\\\\"remove the redundant simple index\\\\\\\" fix is deferred. The code is functionally correct — `listProjectProcessSummaries` uses the compound index, and `by_projectId` is not used within `processes.ts`. Whether `by_projectId` is used by other Convex functions is not confirmed.\\\\n- **Impact:** The `by_projectId` index may be redundant. In Convex, compound indexes can serve single-field equality queries if the compound index's first field matches, so `by_projectId_and_updatedAt` would suffice for both the sorted list and any future by-projectId-only query. Retaining `by_projectId` has negligible runtime cost but is misleading.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Grep for `.withIndex('by_projectId', ...)` across all convex files to confirm whether the simple index is actually referenced. If unreferenced, remove it before or during Story 1.\\\\n\\\\n### F7 — `projectId as Id<'projects'>` type cast in `createProcess`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `processes.ts:70`: `const projectId = args.projectId as Id<'projects'>;` casts a validated `v.string()` argument to a Convex ID type. This is the existing repo pattern for string-typed foreign keys. The bundle acknowledges this as a residual risk.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (acknowledged residual, within scope claim)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `processes.ts:70`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** The `processes` table stores `projectId: v.string()`, so this field is genuinely a string at runtime. The cast is necessary to call `ctx.db.patch(projectId, ...)` on the `projects` table. The Convex guidelines prefer `v.id('projects')` for strong-typed foreign keys, but migrating this is out of Story 0 scope.\\\\n- **Impact:** No runtime error; minor type-safety gap.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Track as tech debt. Future story or migration will align to `v.id()` types.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## COMPLETENESS GAPS\\\\n\\\\n### G1 — `websocketPlugin` does not register `@fastify/websocket`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** The plugin (`websocket.plugin.ts`) only decorates the Fastify instance with a `NoopProcessLiveHub`. It does not call `app.register(websocket, ...)` from `@fastify/websocket`. The tech design specifies that the plugin registers `@fastify/websocket`. This is intentional for Story 0 (scaffolding only), but a future story implementing live connections will need to add this registration step.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (Story 0 scope is scaffold-only)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `websocket.plugin.ts` (full file); tech-design-server.md describes \\\\\\\"Register websocket support\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Impact:** None for Story 0. Story 2 or 3 (live updates) will need to extend this plugin.\\\\n\\\\n### G2 — `processLiveHub` decoration gap in `app.ts`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `app.ts:87`: `const processLiveHub = options.processLiveHub;` — this value may be `undefined`. The `websocketPlugin` is then registered with `{ processLiveHub }` which becomes `{ processLiveHub: undefined }`. The plugin handles `undefined` by falling back to `NoopProcessLiveHub`. However, the Fastify `FastifyInstance.processLiveHub` declaration in `websocket.plugin.ts` is added via plugin, but `app.ts` also declares `processLiveHub` in the `declare module 'fastify'` block on `process-live-hub.ts` — wait, no: `websocket.plugin.ts` owns the Fastify module augmentation for `processLiveHub`. The `declare module 'fastify'` in `app.ts` does NOT include `processLiveHub` — it only includes the project and process service decorations. So the only augmentation is from the plugin, which is correct.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\\\\n- **Evidence:** `app.ts:51–61` (no `processLiveHub` in declare block); `websocket.plugin.ts:8–12` (declares it there)\\\\n- **Impact:** No runtime impact. Correct separation — the hub is a plugin-owned decoration, not a service-owned one.\\\\n- **Validation step:** None required.\\\\n\\\\n### G3 — `bootstrap.ts` loads project shell for `process-work-surface` routes\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `bootstrapApp`'s `loadParsedRoute` function falls into the shell-loading `else` branch for any non-`project-index` route, including `process-work-surface`. This means navigating to a process surface still calls `getProjectShell`. This is existing Epic 1 behavior; Story 0 extends the bootstrap only to seed `processSurface.projectId` and `processSurface.processId` from the route. The shell-loading side effect is not a Story 0 defect.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (future story concern)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `bootstrap.ts:151–234`\\\\n- **Impact:** Story 1 (process surface page) will need to either extend `loadParsedRoute` for `process-work-surface` or tolerate the shell loading alongside surface loading.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Story 1 implementation review should address this.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nNone.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is inaccurate** (F6). The compound index was renamed, not removed; both indexes remain. Correct the bundle description if it feeds downstream records. No code change required.\\\\n\\\\n2. **`by_projectId` index on `processes` may be unreferenced** (F6 follow-on). Grep for usage before Story 1 and remove if dead.\\\\n\\\\n3. **`bootstrap.ts` health endpoint label is stale** (`app.ts:128`: `story: 'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'`). This is existing Epic 1 code not owned by Story 0, but it will mislead future ops debugging.\\\\n\\\\n4. **Reconnect reconciliation test helper is implicit, not exported** (G1 in requirements matrix). `mergeHistoryItems` and `reconnectingProcessSurfaceStateFixture` exist, but no exported `reconcileProcessSurfaceAfterReconnect` helper. Later stories may need to write their own reconciliation assertions. Low risk.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## UNRESOLVED\\\\n\\\\n| Item | Why Unresolved | Suggested Step |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Gate result (typecheck + build) | Commands require shell approval; could not run independently | Bundle claims PASS; cross-check by running `corepack pnpm run typecheck && corepack pnpm run build` in clean shell |\\\\n| Whether `by_projectId` index is live in any other Convex file | grep not run | `grep -r 'by_projectId' convex/` — if no hits, safely remove |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE RESULT\\\\n\\\\n**UNVERIFIED (approval required to run).** Bundle claims both `corepack pnpm run typecheck` and `corepack pnpm run build` passed. All contract schema parse calls in fixtures are runtime validation — if typecheck passed, schema/type coherence across shared contracts, Convex table fields, and service interfaces is confirmed by the TypeScript compiler. There are no obvious type errors visible from file reads.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## After the review: what I noticed but chose not to report\\\\n\\\\n- The `processWorkSurfaceRouteTemplate` constant uses `{projectId}/{processId}` brace style (non-Express). This is declared as `as const` and appears to be a display-only template, not used for routing. The actual routing pattern uses the `:param` style. No issue.\\\\n- The `applyLiveProcessMessage` function has a subtle asymmetry: it updates `live.subscriptionId` and `live.lastSequenceNumber` unconditionally on every processed message, even `error` messages. This means an error message can advance the sequence number, which prevents reprocessing a later remediation message with a lower sequence number if the subscription restarts. This is a Story 2 concern, not Story 0.\\\\n- `processUpsertLiveFixture` in `live-process.ts` uses `runningProcessSurfaceFixture.processId` (a different process than the `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture`). The fixture name does not signal \\\\\\\"cross-process\\\\\\\". A later story test author could be confused. The `buildLiveProcessMessageFixture` helper silently normalises `entityId` from the payload for `process` entity types, which masks this. Not a defect, but naming could be clearer.\\\\n- The `isStaleMessage` guard has an inverted staleness check — it returns `false` (not stale) when `state.live.subscriptionId !== message.subscriptionId`. This means messages from a different subscription are NOT treated as stale and will be applied. A message from an old subscription with a higher sequence number would pass through. The intent may be that subscription changes reset stale tracking. This is potentially a reconnect-coherence gap, but Story 0 does not own reconnect behaviour end-to-end.\\\\n\\\"}}],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"c5e46e6e-09c2-483f-8c9c-6376381fb014\\\"}\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:347:    processHistoryItems: [\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:388:    'processHistoryItems',\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:420:      processHistoryItems: obj.processHistoryItems as ExecutionResult['processHistoryItems'],\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/history-section.reader.ts:3:  processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/history-section.reader.ts:18:    return processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-work-surface.service.ts:22:  processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-work-surface.service.ts:446:      return processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:10:import { ArchiveFinalizationService } from '../archive/archive-finalization.service.js';\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:11:import { buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey } from '../archive/process-history-compat.service.js';\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:23:    private readonly archiveFinalizationService: Pick<\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:53:      await this.archiveAcceptedUserResponse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:89:      await this.archiveAcceptedUserResponse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:140:  private async archiveAcceptedUserResponse(args: {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:151:    await this.archiveFinalizationService.appendFinalizedEntry({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:155:      finalizationKey: buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:158:      sourceObjectId: args.historyItem.historyItemId,\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/04-materials-and-outputs/codex-impl-round-3.jsonl:27:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_12\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,320p' tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"import { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  AuthSessionService,\\\\n  type SessionResolution,\\\\n  sessionCookieName,\\\\n} from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/auth/auth-session.service.js';\\\\nimport { AuthUserSyncService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/auth/auth-user-sync.service.js';\\\\nimport { DefaultProcessWorkSurfaceService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-work-surface.service.js';\\\\nimport { HistorySectionReader } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/history-section.reader.js';\\\\nimport { MaterialsSectionReader } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.js';\\\\nimport { SideWorkSectionReader } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/side-work-section.reader.js';\\\\nimport { ProcessAccessService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-access.service.js';\\\\nimport { InMemoryPlatformStore } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.js';\\\\nimport { ProjectAccessService } from '../../../apps/platform/server/services/projects/project-access.service.js';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  processSummarySchema,\\\\n  projectSummarySchema,\\\\n} from '../../../apps/platform/shared/contracts/index.js';\\\\nimport {\\\\n  currentProcessRequestFixture,\\\\n  earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture,\\\\n  readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture,\\\\n} from '../../fixtures/process-surface.js';\\\\nimport { readyProcessHistoryFixture } from '../../fixtures/process-history.js';\\\\nimport { readyProcessMaterialsFixture } from '../../fixtures/materials.js';\\\\nimport { completedProcessFixture, runningProcessFixture } from '../../fixtures/processes.js';\\\\nimport { readySideWorkFixture } from '../../fixtures/side-work.js';\\\\nimport { buildApp } from '../../utils/build-app.js';\\\\n\\\\nfunction createTestAuthSessionService(resolution: SessionResolution) {\\\\n  class TestAuthSessionService extends AuthSessionService {\\\\n    constructor() {\\\\n      super({\\\\n        workosClient: {} as never,\\\\n        clientId: 'client_test_process_surface_api',\\\\n        cookiePassword: 'story1-process-api-cookie-password-12345',\\\\n        redirectUri: 'http://localhost:5001/auth/callback',\\\\n        loginReturnUri: 'http://localhost:5001/projects',\\\\n      });\\\\n    }\\\\n\\\\n    override async resolveSession(): Promise<SessionResolution> {\\\\n      return resolution;\\\\n    }\\\\n  }\\\\n\\\\n  return new TestAuthSessionService();\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nclass ThrowingHistorySectionReader extends HistorySectionReader {\\\\n  override async read(): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<HistorySectionReader['read']>>> {\\\\n    throw new Error('Process history could not be loaded.');\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nclass ThrowingMaterialsSectionReader extends MaterialsSectionReader {\\\\n  override async read(): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<MaterialsSectionReader['read']>>> {\\\\n    throw new Error('Process materials could not be loaded.');\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nclass ThrowingSideWorkSectionReader extends SideWorkSectionReader {\\\\n  override async read(): Promise<Awaited<ReturnType<SideWorkSectionReader['read']>>> {\\\\n    throw new Error('Side-work summaries could not be loaded.');\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nconst projectSummary = projectSummarySchema.parse({\\\\n  projectId: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.project.projectId,\\\\n  name: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.project.name,\\\\n  ownerDisplayName: 'Lee Moore',\\\\n  role: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.project.role,\\\\n  processCount: 1,\\\\n  artifactCount: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.materials.currentArtifacts.length,\\\\n  sourceAttachmentCount: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.materials.currentSources.length,\\\\n  lastUpdatedAt: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.updatedAt,\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\nconst waitingProcessSummary = processSummarySchema.parse({\\\\n  processId: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.processId,\\\\n  displayLabel: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.displayLabel,\\\\n  processType: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.processType,\\\\n  status: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.status,\\\\n  phaseLabel: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.phaseLabel,\\\\n  nextActionLabel: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.nextActionLabel,\\\\n  availableActions: ['respond'],\\\\n  hasEnvironment: false,\\\\n  updatedAt: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.updatedAt,\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\nconst draftProcessSummary = processSummarySchema.parse({\\\\n  processId: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.processId,\\\\n  displayLabel: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.displayLabel,\\\\n  processType: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.processType,\\\\n  status: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.status,\\\\n  phaseLabel: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.phaseLabel,\\\\n  nextActionLabel: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.nextActionLabel,\\\\n  availableActions: ['open'],\\\\n  hasEnvironment: false,\\\\n  updatedAt: earlyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process.updatedAt,\\\\n});\\\\n\\\\nfunction buildPopulatedStore() {\\\\n  const processArtifact = {\\\\n    artifactId:\\\\n      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts[0]?.artifactId ?? 'artifact-process-001',\\\\n    displayName: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts[0]?.displayName ?? 'Artifact',\\\\n    currentVersionLabel:\\\\n      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts[0]?.currentVersionLabel ?? null,\\\\n    attachmentScope: 'process' as const,\\\\n    processId: waitingProcessSummary.processId,\\\\n    processDisplayLabel: waitingProcessSummary.displayLabel,\\\\n    updatedAt:\\\\n      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentArtifacts[0]?.updatedAt ??\\\\n      waitingProcessSummary.updatedAt,\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  const processSource = {\\\\n    sourceAttachmentId:\\\\n      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.sourceAttachmentId ?? 'source-process-001',\\\\n    displayName: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.displayName ?? 'liminal-build',\\\\n    purpose: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.purpose ?? 'implementation',\\\\n    targetRef: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.targetRef ?? null,\\\\n    hydrationState: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.hydrationState ?? 'hydrated',\\\\n    attachmentScope: 'process' as const,\\\\n    processId: waitingProcessSummary.processId,\\\\n    processDisplayLabel: waitingProcessSummary.displayLabel,\\\\n    updatedAt:\\\\n      readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentSources[0]?.updatedAt ?? waitingProcessSummary.updatedAt,\\\\n  };\\\\n\\\\n  return new InMemoryPlatformStore({\\\\n    accessibleProjectsByUserId: {\\\\n      'user:workos-user-1': [projectSummary],\\\\n    },\\\\n    projectAccessByProjectId: {\\\\n      [projectSummary.projectId]: {\\\\n        kind: 'accessible',\\\\n        project: projectSummary,\\\\n      },\\\\n    },\\\\n    processesByProjectId: {\\\\n      [projectSummary.projectId]: [waitingProcessSummary, draftProcessSummary],\\\\n    },\\\\n    artifactsByProjectId: {\\\\n      [projectSummary.projectId]: [processArtifact],\\\\n    },\\\\n    sourceAttachmentsByProjectId: {\\\\n      [projectSummary.projectId]: [processSource],\\\\n    },\\\\n    processHistoryItemsByProcessId: {\\\\n      [waitingProcessSummary.processId]: readyProcessHistoryFixture.items,\\\\n      [draftProcessSummary.processId]: [],\\\\n    },\\\\n    currentRequestsByProcessId: {\\\\n      [waitingProcessSummary.processId]: currentProcessRequestFixture,\\\\n      [draftProcessSummary.processId]: null,\\\\n    },\\\\n    processOutputsByProcessId: {\\\\n      [waitingProcessSummary.processId]: readyProcessMaterialsFixture.currentOutputs,\\\\n      [draftProcessSummary.processId]: [],\\\\n    },\\\\n    processSideWorkItemsByProcessId: {\\\\n      [waitingProcessSummary.processId]: readySideWorkFixture.items,\\\\n      [draftProcessSummary.processId]: [],\\\\n    },\\\\n  });\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\ndescribe('process work surface api', () => {\\\\n  it('TC-1.2a, TC-1.3a, TC-1.3b, and TC-1.4a return the populated process bootstrap', async () => {\\\\n    const platformStore = buildPopulatedStore();\\\\n    const app = await buildApp({\\\\n      authSessionService: createTestAuthSessionService({\\\\n        actor: {\\\\n          userId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          workosUserId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          email: 'lee@example.com',\\\\n          displayName: 'Lee Moore',\\\\n        },\\\\n        reason: null,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      authUserSyncService: new AuthUserSyncService(platformStore),\\\\n      platformStore,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const response = await app.inject({\\\\n      method: 'GET',\\\\n      url: `/api/projects/${projectSummary.projectId}/processes/${waitingProcessSummary.processId}`,\\\\n      cookies: {\\\\n        [sessionCookieName]: 'valid-session-cookie',\\\\n      },\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    expect(response.statusCode).toBe(200);\\\\n    expect(response.json()).toMatchObject({\\\\n      project: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.project,\\\\n      process: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.process,\\\\n      history: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.history,\\\\n      materials: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.materials,\\\\n      currentRequest: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.currentRequest,\\\\n      sideWork: readyProcessWorkSurfaceFixture.sideWork,\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    await app.close();\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it('TC-1.4b returns stable empty section envelopes for an early process', async () => {\\\\n    const platformStore = buildPopulatedStore();\\\\n    const app = await buildApp({\\\\n      authSessionService: createTestAuthSessionService({\\\\n        actor: {\\\\n          userId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          workosUserId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          email: 'lee@example.com',\\\\n          displayName: 'Lee Moore',\\\\n        },\\\\n        reason: null,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      authUserSyncService: new AuthUserSyncService(platformStore),\\\\n      platformStore,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const response = await app.inject({\\\\n      method: 'GET',\\\\n      url: `/api/projects/${projectSummary.projectId}/processes/${draftProcessSummary.processId}`,\\\\n      cookies: {\\\\n        [sessionCookieName]: 'valid-session-cookie',\\\\n      },\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    expect(response.statusCode).toBe(200);\\\\n    expect(response.json()).toMatchObject({\\\\n      history: {\\\\n        status: 'empty',\\\\n        items: [],\\\\n      },\\\\n      materials: {\\\\n        status: 'empty',\\\\n        currentArtifacts: [],\\\\n        currentOutputs: [],\\\\n        currentSources: [],\\\\n      },\\\\n      sideWork: {\\\\n        status: 'empty',\\\\n        items: [],\\\\n      },\\\\n      currentRequest: null,\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    await app.close();\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it('TC-6.4b omits project data from a forbidden bootstrap response', async () => {\\\\n    const platformStore = new InMemoryPlatformStore({\\\\n      projectAccessByProjectId: {\\\\n        [projectSummary.projectId]: { kind: 'forbidden' },\\\\n      },\\\\n    });\\\\n    const app = await buildApp({\\\\n      authSessionService: createTestAuthSessionService({\\\\n        actor: {\\\\n          userId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          workosUserId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          email: 'lee@example.com',\\\\n          displayName: 'Lee Moore',\\\\n        },\\\\n        reason: null,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      authUserSyncService: new AuthUserSyncService(platformStore),\\\\n      platformStore,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const response = await app.inject({\\\\n      method: 'GET',\\\\n      url: `/api/projects/${projectSummary.projectId}/processes/${waitingProcessSummary.processId}`,\\\\n      cookies: {\\\\n        [sessionCookieName]: 'valid-session-cookie',\\\\n      },\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    expect(response.statusCode).toBe(403);\\\\n    expect(response.json()).toEqual({\\\\n      code: 'PROJECT_FORBIDDEN',\\\\n      message: 'You do not have access to this process.',\\\\n      status: 403,\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    await app.close();\\\\n  });\\\\n\\\\n  it('TC-3.2a, TC-5.1a, and TC-5.2a keep the outstanding attention request visible beside routine progress', async () => {\\\\n    const platformStore = buildPopulatedStore();\\\\n    const app = await buildApp({\\\\n      authSessionService: createTestAuthSessionService({\\\\n        actor: {\\\\n          userId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          workosUserId: 'workos-user-1',\\\\n          email: 'lee@example.com',\\\\n          displayName: 'Lee Moore',\\\\n        },\\\\n        reason: null,\\\\n      }),\\\\n      authUserSyncService: new AuthUserSyncService(platformStore),\\\\n      platformStore,\\\\n    });\\\\n    const response = await app.inject({\\\\n      method: 'GET',\\\\n      url: `/api/projects/${projectSummary.projectId}/processes/${waitingProcessSummary.processId}`,\\\\n      cookies: {\\\\n        [sessionCookieName]: 'valid-session-cookie',\\\\n      },\\\\n    });\\\\n\\\\n    expect(response.statusCode).toBe(200);\\\\n    expect(response.json()).toMatchObject({\\\\n      currentRequest: currentProcessRequestFixture,\\\\n    });\\\\n    expect(response.json().history.items).toEqual(\\\\n      expect.arrayContaining([\\\\n 