t/degradation proof are deferred. Reassess S1-F1 under that ruling, preserve S1-F2 as nonblocking unless it blocks the story-local primitive contract, and return a final verifier outcome suitable for story-lead acceptance or block.\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"selfNote\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"After ruling application, accept only if verifier returns pass with S1-F1 resolved/nonblocking and story/epic gates remain evidenced as passing.\\\\\\\"}\\\"}}\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/story-lead/streams/001-story-lead.stdout.log:19:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_0\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"action\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"run-continue\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Latest verifier result is revise with blocking finding S1-F3: the Story 1 append/read primitive exports are absent and both targeted test and story gate fail. The smallest safe next action is to continue the existing story implementor session to restore the primitive surface and passing gates before any further verification or acceptance.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"inputs\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"continuationRef\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"storyImplementor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"promptAddendum\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Address verifier finding S1-F3 from /Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/014-verify.json. Restore the Story 1 canonical archive-entry primitive exports in convex/archiveEntries.ts: appendArchiveEntry and listArchiveEntries, with the primitive-only scope affirmed by impl-lead ruling 012. Preserve required taxonomy validation, process-scoped finalizationKey idempotency, atomic per-process sequence assignment, stable sequence-ordered reads, related-id round-trip, lifecycleState finalized, and bounded page shape. Do not expand into Story 2/3/6 service/API/enrichment work. Run the targeted Convex archive entries te