/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:295:| TC-5.5b | `tests/service/client/derived-archive-views.test.ts` | `TC-5.5b derived view reports degraded status` | Client renders degraded view |\\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/streams/014-verify.stdout.log:41:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_21\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"artifactsRead\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"reviewScopeSummary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Follow-up convergence under impl-lead ruling 012: rechecked the updated Story 1 scope/mapping docs against the current `convex/archiveEntries` and `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` surfaces, then reran the targeted Story 1 test and the configured story gate to validate current readiness.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"priorFindingStatuses\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"S1-F1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"resolved\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Impl-lead ruling 012 and the updated story/test-plan/tech-design text now consistently judge Story 1 on the primitive append/read boundary only. The story now rewrites AC-1.1 and AC-1.4 to primitive-level behavior and maps TC-1.1a/b/c and TC-1.4a/b to `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:51-97`, `156-178`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:44-54`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:563-569`). The prior scope dispute is closed.\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"S1-F2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"resolved\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"rationale\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The prior `collect()`-then-slice observation no longer applies because the cited `listArchiveEntries` implementation is not present in the current `convex/archiveEntries.ts`. That concern is superseded by the new blocking regression below: the Story 1 append/read primitive exports are now absent entirely.\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"newFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"S1-F3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The current archiveEntries module no longer exports the Story 1 append/read primitive, and the story gate now fails\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"`convex/archiveEntries.ts` currently contains only validators and `archiveEntriesTableFields` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:1-45`); it does not export `appendArchiveEntry` or `listArchiveEntries`. `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` still imports those symbols at `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:1-3`, so the targeted Story 1 test now fails immediately with `_handler` undefined, and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` fails in typecheck with `TS2305: Module './archiveEntries.js' has no exported member 'appendArchiveEntry'` and `listArchiveEntries`. A repo search over `convex` and `apps/platform` found no replacement mutation/query export for these primitive functions. This removes the executable Story 1 persistence surface and breaks the configured story gate.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1c\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.3a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.3b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.4a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.4b\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"same-session-implementor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"openFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"S1-F3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"The current archiveEntries module no longer exports the Story 1 append/read primitive, and the story gate now fails\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"`convex/archiveEntries.ts` currently contains only validators and `archiveEntriesTableFields` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:1-45`); it does not export `appendArchiveEntry` or `listArchiveEntries`. `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts` still imports those symbols at `convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:1-3`, so the targeted Story 1 test now fails immediately with `_handler` undefined, and `corepack pnpm run green-verify` fails in typecheck with `TS2305: Module './archiveEntries.js' has no exported member 'appendArchiveEntry'` and `listArchiveEntries`. A repo search over `convex` and `apps/platform` found no replacement mutation/query export for these primitive functions. This removes the executable Story 1 persistence surface and breaks the configured story gate.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"convex/archiveEntries.test.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1c\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.3a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.3b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.4a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.4b\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"same-session-implementor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"requirementCoverage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"verified\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"unverified\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.1c\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2a\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-1.2b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-1.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"