ice`/`appendFinalizedEntry` or `ArchiveReadService`/`getArchive` implementation under `apps/platform/server/services`, and the only executable proof is the Convex handler test (`convex/archiveEntries.test.ts:196-236`, `370-436`). That leaves finalized user/model/process-event archival and degraded related-context reads without the required story-level evidence.\\\\\\\"]},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"S1-F2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"unresolved\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/artifacts/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence/008-verify.json\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"`listArchiveEntries` reads `by_processId_and_sequence` with `.collect()` and only then slices in `paginateArchiveEntries` (`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155`, `261-280`). The story/design describe this store method as returning one bounded page (`docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/01-canonical-archive-entry-persistence.md:126-127`; `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:661-668`). The outward page contract is correct, but long-process production reads still materialize the full archive in memory.\\\\\\\"]}]},\\\\\\\"riskAndDeviationReview\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"specDeviations\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"assumedRisks\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"scopeChanges\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"productionPathDecisionItems\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"description\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"`convex/archiveEntries.ts:139-155` uses `collect()` plus in-memory slicing for `listArchiveEntries`, so long-process archive reads are not yet bounded at the persistence layer.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reasoning\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Story verifier surfaced a production-path audit note. Verifier outcome, open findings, and explicit story-lead risk decisions determine whether action or caller approval is required.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/a